  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Public Health Operations in Emergencies for National Strengthening in the Indo-Pacific (PHOENIX)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The National Critical Care and Trauma Response Centre (NCCTRC) is strengthening pandemic preparedness and outbreak response systems and capacity in the Indo-Pacific by training public health specialists. Specialists will be trained to rapidly deploy in response to disease outbreaks, both within their countries and across the region. Key areas of focus include national health workforce capacity building; increased coordination and integration within public health emergency systems; regional health workforce capacity building and strengthened networks and enhanced gender equality and inclusion in public health emergency responses.</narrative>
  </description>
